<title>GERMANY: Duesseldorf air cargo up 20.8 pct in February.</title>
<headline>Duesseldorf air cargo up 20.8 pct in February.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total flown air cargo handled at Duesseldorf airport in February rose 20.8 percent to 5,508 tonnes, figures from the German airports association ADV showed.</p>
<p>This was a slight rise on the 19.2 percent growth recorded in January, the monthly ADV traffic report showed.</p>
<p>Exports at Duesseldorf airport picked up to 24.6 percent growth in February after a 17.5 percent rise in January.</p>
<p>But imports slowed slightly to 18.9 percent growth in February following a 20.4 percent increase in January.</p>
<p>The following tables show cargo handled at Duesseldorf airport in February and for the year to date in tonnes and with year-on-year percentage changes.</p>
<p>    Feb 1997			Monthly total	Pct change</p>
<p>    Total flown cargo		5,508		Up   20.8</p>
<p>    Exports			    2,464		Up   24.6</p>
<p>    Imports			    2,919		Up   18.9</p>
<p>    Transit				125		     n/a</p>
<p>    Jan-Feb 1997		 Cumulative total    Pct change</p>
<p>    Total flown cargo	     10,436		Up   20.0</p>
<p>    Exports			    4,594		Up   21.2</p>
<p>    Imports			    5,572		Up   19.6</p>
<p>    Transit				270		     n/a</p>
<p>Source: German Airports Association ADV, market research dept.</p>
<p>--Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
